{
  "kind": "classes",
  "title": "F126.3.4 start, follow and stop a run: the interface design",
  "caption": "The judge hands back a mark with its cost and a turn keeps it. The rows carry the costs and the estimate. The desk can stop the run it plays. The web's client starts and stops a run for the card and the page. The number is the step; violet is there already and unchanged.",
